      "id": 125455,
      "name": "dlott1988",
      "username": "dlott1988",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dlott1988/{size}/2135_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-01-07T17:21:22.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"phantaskippy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/48/1897_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> phantaskippy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>One ouch found.End of turn effects are not resolved in order of player choice. &nbsp;Start and End of turn effects are resolved in the order the cards entered play.It is nice to see these mistakes in your videos because 90% of the time when I play a game I do something wrong.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Scott \"Tox\" Morris and I were talking about that. He accused Christopher of the same misstep. I blame the amazingly engaging nature of the game. I'm just a overwhelmed by the onslaught of awesome that I overlook a simple rule or math operation.</p>\n<p>I also have a very laid back attitude about games. You bought it, you play it the way you want. If that's by the book, go for it. If that's with home brews and variants, have a blast.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>We usually kangaroo court what card would trigger first; \"Baron Blade would hit first he's mad at Legacy for Thoking him.\"</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
